.SH REGULAR EXPRESSIONS
An expression list file contains regular expressions with one regular expression per line. The command guard uses Posix regular expressions.  The Posix Regular Expression language is a notation for describing textual patterns. Of most interest is:

.TP
\fB.\fR Matches any single character (use "\." to match a ".").

.TP
\fB[abc]\fR Matches one of the characters ("[abc]" matches a single "a" or "b" or  "c").

.TP
\fB[c-g]\fR Matches one of the characters in the range ("[c-g]" matches a single "c" or "d" or  "e" or "f" or "g". "[a-z0-9]" matches any single letter or digit. "[-/.:?]" matches any single "-" or "/" or "." or ":" or "?".).

.TP
\fB?\fR None or one of the preceding ("words?" will match "word" and "words". "[abc]?" matches a single "a" or "b" or "c" or nothing (i.e. "")).

.TP
\fB*\fR None or more of the preceding ("words*" will match "words" and "wordsssssss". ".*" will match anything including nothing).

.TP
\fB+\fR One or more of the preceding ("xxx+" will match a sequence of 3 or more "x").

.TP
\fB(expr1|expr2)\fR One of the expressions, which in turn may contain a similar construction ("(foo|bar)" will match "foo" or "bar". "(foo|bar)?" will match "foo" or "bar" or nothing (i.e. "")).

.TP
\fB$\fR The end of the line ("(foo|bar)$" will match "foo" or "bar" only at the end of a line).

.TP
\fB\\x\fR Disable the special meaning of x where x is one of the special regex characters \fB".?*+()^$[]{}\\"\fR (\\. will match a single ".", "\\\\" a single "\\" etc.)

.SH AUTO UPDATES ON A MANAGER SYSTEM
On a \fImanager\fR system, the automatic URL lists update can be activated depending on the installed license level. The activation is normally possible for non-free installation only. This feature on a manager allows you to periodically download URL lists from one or more remote file servers and then automatically push them on all remote gateways. Please refer to the \fBmanager\fR command for further information.

If on a manager, an automatic URL list download is configured to download updates (diff files and not the complete content) and after a successful download from a remote file server, its push to a remote gateway fails (because of an unavailability of that gateway at the time of the push operation), the next time (the day or week after) the system will download and push the complete content for that URL list.

